"""
## Purpose and audience
Deliberately-RED probe (R2 lane): this file MUST fail. It exists so the test
runner's RED reporting, verdict recording, and downstream verdict consumers
have a stable failing signal to be verified against. Audience: maintainers of
the test runner and anyone wiring up verdict pipelines.
## Operator workflow
Run this file alone and confirm the verdict is a single failing scenario:
`./src/compiler_rust/target/bootstrap/simple run test/unit/compiler/r2_probe_fail_spec.spl`
## Compatibility and limitations
The failure is the contract: scenario "must report RED" asserts a product
result against a deliberately wrong expected value and must keep failing. Do
not "fix" the assertion to pass — that would silence the probe. The asserted
value comes from a real product call (text length) so the probe exercises the
runner's assertion path, not a literal-only comparison.
## Verification guidance and troubleshooting
A GREEN verdict on this file means the probe was weakened or the runner stopped
executing scenario bodies — treat that as a runner regression. A load error
before the assertion means the file itself broke; restore the probe shape.
"""
# Lifecycle: doc/01_research/compiler/compiler_internals/compiler_compile_options_field_access.md ;
# doc/03_plan/compiler/forwarding/zero_cost_layers_c0_c5_staged_implementation_plan_2026-08-07.md ;
# doc/04_architecture/language/simple_feature_module.md ;
# doc/05_design/language/language_features/syntax_features/pipeline_operators_design.md
# @manual_section: deliberate_red_probes

use std.spec.{describe, it, expect, step}

describe "R2 deliberate fail probe":
    it "must report RED on a deliberately wrong expectation":
        # @req REQ-R2PROBE-001
        # The probe asserts a real product result (text length is 3) against a
        # deliberately wrong expected value, so the failure flows through the
        # runner's full assert/verdict path instead of a literal-only compare.
        step("Assert a real product result against a deliberately wrong value")
        val deliberate_red_product_result = "RED".len()
        expect(deliberate_red_product_result).to_equal(2)  # oracle: the probe contract requires RED; text len 3 vs expected 2 must fail
